Presented with substernal chest pain after a motor-vehicle collision. ECG showed sinus tachycardia without ST elevation. High-sensitivity troponin was 7 ng/L and repeat was 6 ng/L. CT chest showed no acute traumatic injury. Discharged with acetaminophen and return precautions.

