Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, GOLD group B, without acute exacerbation. Spirometry shows FEV1 1.62 L (58% predicted), FVC 2.91 L, and FEV1/FVC 0.56. Resting oxygen saturation is 94% on room air. Continue tiotropium two inhalations daily and albuterol as needed. A 6 mm right upper-lobe pulmonary nodule is unchanged on CT chest.

