A 7 x 5 mm asymmetric pigmented papule on the left upper back was sampled by shave biopsy after local anesthesia with 1% lidocaine with epinephrine. Differential diagnosis includes dysplastic nevus versus melanoma. Hemostasis achieved with aluminum chloride. Wound care instructions were reviewed. Continue triamcinolone 0.1% ointment for plaque psoriasis on the elbows.

