Six weeks after right total knee arthroplasty. Incision is healed without erythema or drainage. Range of motion is 0 to 112 degrees. Radiographs show well-aligned components without loosening or periprosthetic fracture. Continue weight bearing as tolerated and outpatient physical therapy. Use acetaminophen for pain and aspirin 81 mg twice daily until prophylaxis is complete.

